      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This is a complex philosophical debate, so your report should avoid declaring one side objectively \"correct.\" Instead, you can present the concept of \"living heritage\" as the necessary middle ground. Argue that while core elements of identity provide stability, a truly vibrant community requires resilience and the ability to incorporate external influences. Conclude by recommending that preservation efforts focus on protecting *sites and narratives* (tangible anchors) rather than defending against *societal change* itself.",
      "source": "target",
